ers/enigmaticrex/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"89c474a61cfc675fe91f625e5b0ba246a669b1cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sainsaji/EVO-PLAYER-PS5/commits/89c474a61cfc675fe91f625e5b0ba246a669b1cc","html_url":"https://github.com/sainsaji/EVO-PLAYER-PS5/commit/89c474a61cfc675fe91f625e5b0ba246a669b1cc"}]},"merge_base_commit":{"sha":"586ca6d3ca6b41309f6ab4a16da055e712b2121c","node_id":"C_kwDOTzGnatoAKDU4NmNhNmQzY2E2YjQxMzA5ZjZhYjRhMTZkYTA1NWU3MTJiMjEyMWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"sain.saji","email":"sain.sajix@gmail.com","date":"2026-09-05T08:42:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"sain.saji","email":"sain.sajix@gmail.com","date":"2026-09-05T08:42:46Z"},"message":"#37 fix: NATIVE refuses to play instead of falling back to FFmpeg\n\nHardware pass caught it: NATIVE was silently playing an unsupported-codec\n4K clip on FFmpeg — identical to AUTO's graceful degrade, which made the\nswitch a no-op. The previous commit's toast wasn't enough; the user's\ncall is right — a hard preference has to actually refuse, not just\nnarrate what it's about to do anyway.\n\n- start_video_playback(): when NATIVE was requested but evo_vdec_open()'s\n  *chosen backend disagrees (unsupported codec, failed probe, or a native\n  bring-up error), close the FFmpeg decoder it already opened, show\n  \"NATIVE DECODE UNSUPPORTED\" via prospero_codec_error(), and\n  stop_video_playback() + return — same shape as a genuine decoder-init\n  failure. Nothing plays; the user opens Settings and switches to Auto or\n  FFmpeg themselves.\n- prospero_playback_finished_update(): the #57 retry-once-on-FFmpeg for a\n  mid-stream native fatal is now skipped when the preference is NATIVE —\n  it falls through to the ordinary SCREEN_PLAYBACK_FINISHED path instead\n  of quietly finishing the file on software.\n- AUTO and FFMPEG are unaffected — AUTO's whole point is the graceful\n  degrade evo_vdec_open() already provides; this only changes what NATIVE\n  does with a disagreement.\n- docs/evo-pro/native-decode-plan.md and docs/validation.md updated to\n  match; validation.md records the first hardware pass's finding as the\n  reason for this fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"50303209dff5585d6b8dc98b6fbbae336c7570b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sainsaji/EVO-PLAYER-PS5/git/trees/50303209dff5585d6b8dc98b6fbbae336c7570b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sainsaji/EVO-PLAYER-PS5/git/commits/586ca6d3ca6b41309f6ab4a16da055e712b2121c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sainsaji/EVO-PLAYER-PS5/commits/586ca6d3ca6b41309f6ab4a16da055e712b2121c","html_url":"https://github.com/sainsaji/EVO-PLAYER-PS5/commit/586ca6d3ca6b41309f6ab4a16da055e712b2121c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sainsaji/EVO-PLAYER-PS5/commits/586ca6d3ca6b41309f6ab4a16da055e712b2121c/comments","author":{"login":"enigmaticrex","id":56771208,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NzcxMjA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56771208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex","html_url":"https://github.com/enigmaticrex","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex